---
name: cycle-anchor-drift-monitor
description: Multi-month KPI cycle anchor invariants — intra-year uniqueness, oldest-row-wins repair, and prevention trigger (ADR-090)
type: constraint
---
`kpis.frequency_cycle_start` is an INTRA-YEAR invariant: all rows in a
`(employee_id, kpi_name, review_year, frequency)` tuple MUST share the same
anchor. Enforced by trigger `trg_enforce_intra_year_cycle_anchor_consistency`
(BEFORE INSERT). UPDATEs are intentionally exempt so the repair RPC and admin
propagation paths can converge anchors.

**Repair contract.** When divergence is found (existing pre-ADR-090 drift),
use `public.repair_intra_year_cycle_anchor_drift(p_dry_run, p_safety_ceiling)`.
Strategy: oldest-row-wins (smallest `created_at`, ties by id ASC). Only
`frequency_cycle_start` is mutated. Every change writes
`kpi_audit_logs.action='KPI_CYCLE_ANCHOR_REPAIRED'` with
`metadata.policy='ADR-090'`, `metadata.strategy='oldest_row_wins'`. Safety
ceiling defaults to 500 rows. Repair is reversible from the audit log.

**Detector.** `public.detect_intra_year_cycle_anchor_drift()` returns one row
per drifted tuple (anchors[] + affected_row_count). Cheap GROUP BY HAVING;
safe to call from a daily monitor.

**Pure-helper SSOT.** `src/lib/cycleAnchorRepair.ts::planAnchorRepairs`
mirrors the RPC selection rule and is the only place to evolve the strategy
— tests in `src/test/cycleAnchorRepairSelection.test.ts` lock it down (Sajid
Bi-Monthly Feb-Mar + Abhas Half-Yearly Apr-Sep regression cases).

**Anti-pattern.** Do NOT call `public.resolve_cycle_anchor(frequency, month_idx)`
(2-arg) on rows that already have an anchor — it returns Jan-anchored
windows and overwrites legitimate offset cycles. Always use the 3-arg
sticky overload `(frequency, month_idx, existing_anchor)` per ADR-088.

